{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419715-data-corr-altering-stored-info-no-forces","id":1419715,"title":"Data/Corr, altering stored info, No Forces?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-22T21:56:23-07:00","id":1419715,"title":"Data/Corr, altering stored info, No Forces?","content":"I was watching the Technocracy Reloaded kickstarter chronicle on YouTube. The storyteller is one of the writers. They were talking about using Correspondence to move data around on the internet, alter it, etc. It seemed pretty clear that you do this with Correspondence alone. <br /> <br /> My question is, what about Forces? I'm not saying you shouldn't be able to use Correspondence or its equivalent to alter stored information. Otherwise, a Virtual Adept character's affinity Sphere doesn't apply to what they actually do. It's just that, in practical terms, computer data is made up of electric charges on a hard drive somewhere. <br /> <br /> If a Forces Mage with no Correspondence has line of sight to a computer, shouldn't he be able to do the same, given two or three points in Computers? If he's logged into the internet he should, theoretically, be able alter data stored somewhere else without Correspondence because he is manipulating a Forces Pattern that is connected to the device at the other end, moving at the speed of electricity (or light through fiber optic cables).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-22T22:33:23-07:00","id":1419720,"title":"","content":"I have no problem using Forces to manipulate information; but it should take more successes that way than it takes to use Data or Correspondence to manipulate information. This is a more general principle as I see it: a player can use any Sphere for any Effect of you can justify it; but if the Storyteller thinks that the fit isn't the best, he can increase the number of successes needed to achieve the result. Want to use Life to mess with someone's emotions? Go for it; but it should require more successes to do this than to use Mind to mess with someone's emotions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-23T00:52:15-07:00","id":1419734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419715-data-corr-altering-stored-info-no-forces?p=1419720#post1419720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no problem using Forces to manipulate information; but it should take more successes that way than it takes to use Data or Correspondence to manipulate information. This is a more general principle as I see it: a player can use any Sphere for any Effect of you can justify it; but if the Storyteller thinks that the fit isn't the best, he can increase the number of successes needed to achieve the result.</div> </div> </div> </div>How convenient. I'm the storyteller. The Cabal doesn't have Correspondence (thank Gaia for a self-contained setting). The Hermetic will be able to alter computer data with Forces. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1419715-data-corr-altering-stored-info-no-forces?p=1419720#post1419720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Want to use Life to mess with someone's emotions? Go for it; but it should require more successes to do this than to use Mind to mess with someone's emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I rule, Life can be used to induce sexual excitation, but not determine who the target seeks out. Of course, if you have Life 3, you can make yourself the hottest person in the room. I allow Life to induce muscle relaxation, calming a would-be attacker. Mind is an overpowered Sphere. With Mind 4, you can basically conscript Mages from the opposing faction, altering their previous beliefs to something compatible with your own faction's paradigm - and they don't even remember it happened. I limit this quite a bit.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}